{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-45f5a40f-5cd2-4373-87bc-82c72335e69e","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-9e0f582ce7f1c571","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9020-fwig8g3z/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E002.md","content":"# Productize supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic productizes a supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime for the models cleared by the AMD Instinct validation campaign, making ROCm an officially supported accelerator option for model serving alongside the existing CUDA builds. It builds the ROCm variant of the vLLM runtime image in the existing midstream serving runtimes repo, wires it into the platform's serving runtime support, and validates that it serves through the standard KServe deployment flow on AMD GPU nodes.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Build the vLLM ROCm runtime image variant in the existing midstream vLLM repo, following the same build and release process as the productized CUDA runtime images.\n- Pin the upstream ROCm base/runtime image version to one that aligns with the target platform release train, and record the alignment decision.\n- Define the supported ServingRuntime configuration for the ROCm vLLM variant covering the cleared model list, including the AMD GPU resource requirements (amd.com/gpu) for accelerator assignment.\n- Productize the runtime for exactly the models cleared by the validation campaign's go/no-go scope.\n- Validate that the ROCm runtime serves through the standard KServe InferenceService and ServingRuntime flow (KServe itself requires no code changes — this is a validation of the passive component, not a modification of it).\n- Ensure the ROCm image build is released through the standard serving runtimes build pipeline.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The vLLM ROCm runtime image builds and is released through the standard serving runtimes build pipeline, with the pipeline green for the release build.\n- The pinned upstream ROCm image version and its release-train alignment are documented in the epic's deliverable.\n- A ServingRuntime configuration for the ROCm vLLM variant exists and is supported for every model on the cleared list, and no model outside the cleared list is advertised as supported.\n- A model from the cleared list is served via a standard KServe InferenceService using the ROCm runtime on AMD GPU nodes, with the InferenceService reaching Ready status and serving inference requests successfully (KServe passive-component validation).\n- The supported scope (models, hardware, driver level) is recorded for handoff to documentation.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-2 (P0): A supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime is productized for the models the validation campaign clears.\n\n## Risks\n\n- Upstream ROCm image release cadence is controlled by AMD and the upstream communities (strategy open question 2); if no upstream image version aligns with the target release train, the pinned version and release timing must be renegotiated. This is an alignment risk on this epic's deliverable, not a gate on starting the work.\n\n## Notes\n\n- The scope of this epic (which models are productized) is determined by the validation campaign's go/no-go outcome: a partial clear narrows the model list; a full no-go removes this epic's work. The campaign's validated report and cleared model list are prerequisites.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":31482,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ae484d814cc53cc0","agent_id":"a3010f8686c837bb3","session_id":"fe501be6-c4a7-499a-b593-08b3eb0d5405","uuid":"b20af360-5568-4242-a419-8ae0c3b2f81a","timestamp":"2026-10-25T19:12:34.029Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9020"}
