{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-9c94522e-759d-4198-bd6c-3765bedc62b5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-993b29ae1937015d","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9020-fwig8g3z/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E003.md","content":"# PyTorch ROCm training support with Kueue admission and amd.com/gpu quota\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic makes PyTorch training on ROCm a supported capability for single- and multi-GPU jobs admitted through Kueue, including handling of the amd.com/gpu resource in the queueing and quota model. It extends the Distributed Workloads stack's supported accelerator resources beyond NVIDIA GPUs so that PyTorchJobs using PyTorch ROCm runtime images can be queued, admitted with gang semantics, and accounted against amd.com/gpu quota.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Enable amd.com/gpu as a supported quota resource in the Distributed Workloads queueing configuration (ClusterQueue/LocalQueue resource flavors), mirroring the existing NVIDIA GPU quota handling.\n- Validate that single-GPU and multi-GPU PyTorchJobs running PyTorch ROCm images are admitted through Kueue with all-or-nothing (gang) semantics on AMD GPU nodes.\n- Validate the Training Operator path for ROCm jobs (PyTorchJob CRD with ROCm container images and amd.com/gpu resource requests — the Training Operator itself requires no code changes; this is a validation of the passive component).\n- Document the supported job shapes (single- and multi-GPU) and any constraints discovered for multi-node ROCm training.\n- Validate quota accounting: jobs consuming amd.com/gpu are charged against the configured quota and queue correctly when quota is exhausted.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A ClusterQueue/LocalQueue configuration supporting amd.com/gpu quota exists and is validated.\n- A single-GPU PyTorchJob using a PyTorch ROCm image is admitted through Kueue and runs to completion on an AMD GPU node.\n- A multi-GPU PyTorchJob using a PyTorch ROCm image is admitted through Kueue with gang semantics (all pods ready before admission completes) and runs to completion.\n- Quota accounting for amd.com/gpu is demonstrated: a job exceeding available quota stays pending and is admitted only when quota is available.\n- The supported job shapes and configuration requirements for PyTorch ROCm training are recorded for handoff to documentation.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-3 (P1): PyTorch training on ROCm is supported for single- and multi-GPU jobs admitted through Kueue, with amd.com/gpu quota handling.\n\n## Risks\n\n- Validation of the supported job shapes requires access to AMD Instinct nodes; hardware availability (strategy open question 1) may delay the validation runs, though the configuration work proceeds independently.\n\n## Notes\n\n- This epic spans the Distributed Workloads component (quota/admission changes and validation — the epic's assigned component) and the Training Operator component (validation only, no code changes; same owning team).\n- Uses upstream PyTorch ROCm images as published; no upstream contribution is required from this strategy.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32290,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ae484d814cc53cc0","agent_id":"a3010f8686c837bb3","session_id":"fe501be6-c4a7-499a-b593-08b3eb0d5405","uuid":"ff10b824-892f-457e-82b0-98f045deb6e7","timestamp":"2026-10-25T19:12:44.719Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9020"}
