ion by the validation campaign.\n- The documented driver prerequisites and hardware requirements match the environment validated during the campaign and productization.\n- All documentation is technically reviewed against the implemented productized runtime and training support by the owning engineering teams, with review sign-off recorded.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-4 (P2): Documentation states supported AMD hardware, driver prerequisites, and the validated model list.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Epic priority is P1 per the docs-authoring priority exception (strategy frontmatter `priority: Major`), not the P2 of the underlying HLR.\n- Depends on the validation campaign (for the validated model list and hardware data), the serving runtime productization, and the training support work, since the documentation describes their outcomes.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":33063,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ae484d814cc53cc0","agent_id":"a3010f8686c837bb3","session_id":"fe501be6-c4a7-499a-b593-08b3eb0d5405","uuid":"00d3017f-f001-4227-b0f0-2d8b438643ca","timestamp":"2026-10-25T19:12:53.321Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9020"}
