rformance notes from the parity data.\n45\t- PyTorch training on ROCm: supported job shapes (single- and multi-GPU), Kueue admission with amd.com/gpu quota configuration, and example job specifications.\n46\t- Limitations: explicitly state what is not supported (other accelerator families, AMD GPU sharing/partitioning) per the strategy's out-of-scope boundaries.\n47\t\n48\t## Acceptance Criteria\n49\t\n50\t- Documentation topics covering supported AMD hardware, driver prerequisites, the validated model list, and PyTorch ROCm training configuration are authored and published through the Red Hat docs content process.\n51\t- The documented model list matches exactly the models cleared for productization by the validation campaign.\n52\t- The documented driver prerequisites and hardware requirements match the environment validated during the campaign and productization.\n53\t- All documentation is technically reviewed against the implemented productized runtime and training support by the owning engineering teams, with review sign-off recorded.\n54\t\n55\t## HLR Traceability\n56\t\n57\t- HLR-4 (P2): Documentation states supported AMD hardware, driver prerequisites, and the validated model list.\n58\t\n59\t## Notes\n60\t\n61\t- Epic priority is P1 per the docs-authoring priority exception (strategy frontmatter `priority: Major`), not the P2 of the underlying HLR.\n62\t- Depends on the validation campaign (for the validated model list and hardware data), the serving runtime productization, and the training support work, since the documentation describes their outcomes.\n63\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b8514bdcd6f1b742","agent_id":"a10a83694d4bb48b5","session_id":"fe501be6-c4a7-499a-b593-08b3eb0d5405","uuid":"a6625ba6-d18c-42e7-9654-089df1e4ddc5","timestamp":"2026-10-25T19:20:25.753Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b61bc7004ea2ba13","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose",