 the serving productization and training support work.\n44\t\n45\t## Scope\n46\t\n47\tContent outline (topics to be authored within this epic's scope):\n48\t\n49\t- Supported AMD hardware: the supported AMD Instinct accelerator models and node requirements for both serving and training.\n50\t- Driver prerequisites: the required ROCm driver levels and installation/verification guidance for cluster administrators.\n51\t- Validated model list: the models cleared by the validation campaign and productized for ROCm serving, with any per-model performance notes from the parity data.\n52\t- PyTorch training on ROCm: supported job shapes (single- and multi-GPU), Kueue admission with amd.com/gpu quota configuration, and example job specifications.\n53\t- Limitations: explicitly state what is not supported (other accelerator families, AMD GPU sharing/partitioning) per the strategy's out-of-scope boundaries.\n54\t\n55\t## Acceptance Criteria\n56\t\n57\t- Documentation topics covering supported AMD hardware, driver prerequisites, the validated model list, and PyTorch ROCm training configuration are authored and published through the Red Hat docs content process.\n58\t- The documented model list matches exactly the models cleared for productization by the validation campaign.\n59\t- The documented driver prerequisites and hardware requirements match the environment validated during the campaign and productization.\n60\t- All documentation is technically reviewed against the implemented productized runtime and training support by the owning engineering teams, with review sign-off recorded.\n61\t\n62\t## HLR Traceability\n63\t\n64\t- HLR-4 (P2): Documentation states supported AMD hardware, driver prerequisites, and the validated model list.\n65\t\n66\t## Notes\n67\t\n68\t- Epic priority is P1 per the docs-authoring priority exception (strategy frontmatter `priority: Major`), not the P2 of the underlying HLR.\n69\t- Depends on the validation campaign (for the validated model list and hardware data), the serving runtime productization, and the training support work, since the documentation describes their outcomes.\n70\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b2af2e29c81a4d5d","agent_id":"a403baa3d0b94eac1","session_id":"fe501be6-c4a7-499a-b593-08b3eb0d5405","uuid":"dfe9edee-e3fb-47fa-b936-861acc90bc27","timestamp":"2026-10-25T19:22:44.290Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a89a18b219fb471c","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9020 decomposition"}
